{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01MX:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "01MX", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA graded ring map <MATH_0001> does not always give rise to a morphism of\nassociated projective homogeneous spectra. The reason is that\nthe inverse image <MATH_0002>\nof a homogeneous prime <MATH_0003> may\ncontain the irrelevant prime <MATH_0004> even if <MATH_0005> does not\ncontain <MATH_0006>.\nThe correct result is stated as follows.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$\\psi : A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\psi^{-1}(\\mathfrak q)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathfrak q \\subset B$", "MATH_0004": "$A_{+}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0006": "$B_{+}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:34c848552ba92bc6df87689b3fb96afaa858db9fa598314d8f3af10a996d5aa3", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:303949deba1f21c2c24909663116d92c8878d9bb2996f9aa54a8065156600d54", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c4cdf0cc246cc0431a2a1062e5574560da82b35da1ef00742a539c2dbc4831b7"}
